Researchers compare the number of potato chips children eat while watching two types of movies. The first type is shown at 8:00 a.m. and the second at 11:00 a.m.; the researchers attribute differences in chip consumption to movie type.

Identify:

a. the explanatory variable;

b. the response variable;

c. one obvious confounding variable.

A shop sold 226 ice creams, summarized below.

| Container | Chocolate | Vanilla | Swirl | Strawberry | Total |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Cup | 20 | 6 | 17 | 4 | 47 |
| Cone | 82 | 12 | 70 | 15 | 179 |
| Total | 102 | 18 | 87 | 19 | 226 |

Find:

a. the probability of a cup;

b. the probability of chocolate or swirl;

c. the probability of chocolate and a cup;

d. the probability of strawberry given a cone;

e. the probability of not chocolate.

Among 100 nurses, 29 live alone and rent, 21 live alone and own, 35 do not live alone and rent, and 15 do not live alone and own. Find the probability of:

a. renting or living alone;

b. owning or not living alone;

c. renting or not living alone.
